# BOEntry Page: Invoice Lines Panel — Implementation Plan

# BOEntry Page: Invoice Lines Panel — Implementation Plan

This document describes the planned implementation approach for migrating the **Invoice Lines Panel** from the legacy ASP.NET Web Forms pages to a Vue.js 3 component (`web/src/views/domain/archive/bo-entry/partials/bo-entry-invoice-line-panel.vue`).

**Companion document:** `BOEntry-Invoice-Lines-Panel-Controls-Relationships.md` (controls inventory, country-specific VAT behavior, cross-panel relationships, and Figma design mapping).

> **Status**: In progress — Phases 1–6 complete, Phase 7 complete (cross-panel integration), Phase 9 remaining.

---

## Table of Contents

- [1. Component Overview](#1-component-overview)
- [2. Props & Context](#2-props--context)
- [3. Template Structure](#3-template-structure)
  - [3.1 Edit Mode](#31-edit-mode)
  - [3.2 Read-Only (View) Mode](#32-read-only-view-mode)
- [4. Invoice Line Data Model](#4-invoice-line-data-model)
- [5. Reactive Behavior](#5-reactive-behavior)
- [6. Phase 1 — Data Model & API](#6-phase-1--data-model--api)
  - [6.1 Extend BoEntryDocument Interface](#61-extend-boentry-document-interface)
  - [6.2 Extend C# Backend](#62-extend-c-backend)
- [7. Phase 2 — Column Visibility Logic](#7-phase-2--column-visibility-logic)
- [8. Phase 3 — Core Invoice Lines Component (Purchase Invoice)](#8-phase-3--core-invoice-lines-component-purchase-invoice)
- [9. Phase 4 — Sales Invoice Columns](#9-phase-4--sales-invoice-columns)
- [10. Phase 5 — Belgium-Specific Features](#10-phase-5--belgium-specific-features)
- [11. Phase 6 — Amount Calculations & Prefill](#11-phase-6--amount-calculations--prefill)
- [12. Phase 7 — Cross-Panel Integration (Complete)](#12-phase-7--cross-panel-integration-complete)
- [13. Phase 8 — Read-Only Mode](#13-phase-8--read-only-mode)
- [14. Translation Keys](#14-translation-keys)
- [15. Testing Strategy](#15-testing-strategy)
- [16. Files to Create / Modify](#16-files-to-create--modify)
- [17. Implementation Checklist](#17-implementation-checklist)
- [18. Deferred Items](#18-deferred-items)
- [19. PR Strategy](#19-pr-strategy)
- [20. Detailed Phase Content](#20-detailed-phase-content)
- [21. Glossary](#21-glossary)
- [Appendix A: Figma Component References](#appendix-a-figma-component-references)
- [Appendix B: Legacy File Reference](#appendix-b-legacy-file-reference)
- [Appendix C: Additional Resources](#appendix-c-additional-resources)

---

## 1. Component Overview

The Invoice Lines Panel is a **dynamic table panel** that displays invoice line items with columns that vary by document type and country. It has two visual states:

- **Edit mode** (`BoEntryMode.Create` / `BoEntryMode.Edit`): Editable table rows with text inputs, dropdowns, number inputs, checkboxes, and delete buttons. Includes "Add line" button and footer with total/invoice amount comparison.
- **View (read-only) mode** (`BoEntryMode.View`): Static text display of all line values. Add/delete buttons hidden.

The Invoice Lines Panel is **only shown for invoice document types**. Visibility is controlled by `hasInvoicePanels` in `bo-entry.vue`:

```ts
const hasInvoicePanels = computed<boolean>(() =>
    [DocumentType.PurchaseInvoice, DocumentType.SalesInvoicePrescanned, DocumentType.ExpenseReport].includes(document.value.type)
);
```

### Current State

The component currently exists as a **placeholder stub**:

```vue
<!-- web/src/views/domain/archive/bo-entry/partials/bo-entry-invoice-line-panel.vue -->
<template>
    <div class="s-invoice-line-panel u-p16">Invoice line panel</div>
</template>
<script setup lang="ts"></script>
```

### File Locations

| Artifact | Path |
|---|---|
| Component | `web/src/views/domain/archive/bo-entry/partials/bo-entry-invoice-line-panel.vue` |
| Unit tests | `web/src/views/domain/archive/bo-entry/partials/bo-entry-invoice-line-panel.spec.ts` (new) |
| Invoice line types | `web/src/views/domain/archive/bo-entry/types/invoiceLine.ts` (new) |
| Column visibility composable | `web/src/views/domain/archive/bo-entry/hooks/useInvoiceLineColumns.ts` (new) |
| Calculation utilities | `web/src/views/domain/archive/bo-entry/utils/invoiceLineCalculations.ts` (new) |
| Data model | `web/src/repositories/backoffice/backoffice.types.ts` (existing) |
| Mapper | `web/src/views/domain/archive/bo-entry/utils/boEntryMapper.ts` (existing) |

---

## 2. Props & Context

The component uses **no props or emits** — all data flows through the injected `BoEntryContext`:

```ts
import { t } from "@/utils/translations/translator";
import { useBoEntryContext } from "@/views/domain/archive/bo-entry/hooks/useBoEntryContext";

const { document, isViewMode } = useBoEntryContext();
```

> **Note**: Follow the pattern from `bo-entry-document-panel.vue` and `bo-entry-other-panel.vue` — use `useBoEntryContext()` which exposes `isViewMode` as a pre-built computed ref.

### CSS Classes

Follow the established convention: `class="s-invoice-line-panel flex flex-c gap8 u-p16"` with `<h3>` for section title.

### Context Data Required

| Data | Source | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `document.invoiceLines` | `BoEntryDocument` | Array of invoice line objects (to be added) |
| `document.type` | `BoEntryDocument` | Determines column visibility |
| `isViewMode` | `BoEntryContext` | Controls edit vs read-only rendering |
| `legislationCountry` | Company context / domain | Determines country-specific columns (BE, ES) |
| `multipleVatCodesEnabled` | Company context / domain | Determines VAT Code column visibility (Purchase Invoice) |
| `isVatSubjected` | Company context / domain | Determines amount labels and VAT field visibility |

---

