**Update mapping in `BackofficeDocumentService.UpdateDocument()`:**

> **Important:** The legacy ASPX code uses an **ID-preserving upsert** pattern — it edits existing lines in-place by their ID, only deletes lines that were explicitly removed by the user, and only calls `AddInvoiceLine()` for truly new lines. The migrated code must follow the same pattern to preserve `TransactionLine.InvoiceLine` foreign key references and avoid orphaning related records.
>
> Reference: `PurchaseInvoiceDocument.BoEntry.aspx` lines 1908–1944 — checks `InvoiceLines.ContainsKey(lineID)` → calls `EditInvoiceLine(lineID, ...)` for existing lines, `AddInvoiceLine(...)` only for new lines, and `SubmitInvoiceLineForDelete(id)` for explicitly deleted lines.

```csharp
// In BackofficeDocumentService.UpdateDocument()
if (input.HasInvoiceLineChanges && document is IInvoiceDocumentBase invoiceDoc)
{
    // 1. Delete lines that were explicitly removed by the user
    if (input.DeletedInvoiceLineIds != null)
    {
        foreach (var deletedId in input.DeletedInvoiceLineIds)
            invoiceDoc.DeleteInvoiceLine(deletedId);
    }

    // 2. Update existing lines in-place or add new lines
    foreach (var lineData in input.InvoiceLines)
    {
        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(lineData.Id)
            && invoiceDoc.InvoiceLines.ContainsKey(lineData.Id))
        {
            // Edit existing line — preserves line ID and foreign key references
            var existingLine = invoiceDoc.InvoiceLines[lineData.Id];
            existingLine.Description.Value = lineData.Description;
            existingLine.Category.Value = lineData.GlAccountId;
            existingLine.TaxCode.Value = lineData.TaxCodeId;
            existingLine.Amount.Value = lineData.Amount;
            existingLine.IncludesTax.Value = lineData.IncludesTax;
            existingLine.DeductableVATPercentage.Value = lineData.DeductableVATPercentage;
        }
        else
        {
            // Add new line — only for lines without an existing ID
            var newLine = invoiceDoc.AddInvoiceLine();
            newLine.Description.Value = lineData.Description;
            newLine.Category.Value = lineData.GlAccountId;
            newLine.TaxCode.Value = lineData.TaxCodeId;
            newLine.Amount.Value = lineData.Amount;
            newLine.IncludesTax.Value = lineData.IncludesTax;
            newLine.DeductableVATPercentage.Value = lineData.DeductableVATPercentage;
        }
    }
}
```

