## 21. Glossary

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **GL Account** | General Ledger Account — the accounting category for the line item. Called "Category" in the backend (`InvoiceLine.Category`). |
| **Tax Code** | VAT code — determines the VAT percentage and type for the line. |
| **Tax Type** | Numeric code derived from Tax Code — determines VAT treatment (e.g., 0=exempt, 5=reverse charge, 11=non-deductible BE). |
| **MultipleVatCodesEnabled** | Domain-level flag (`HasDomainTag("MultipleVATPurchases")`) — when true, each purchase invoice line has its own VAT code. When false, a single VAT code is set at document level. |
| **Deductible VAT %** | Belgium-specific — percentage of VAT that can be deducted. Stored as decimal (0.0–1.0) in backend, displayed as percentage (0–100) in UI. |
| **Professional Deductions** | Belgium-specific backend logic for sole proprietorships — applies `gl.ProfessionalPercentage` to reduce deductible amount. |
| **Inc VAT** | "Includes VAT" checkbox on Sales Invoice lines — when checked, the amount entered includes VAT. |
| **Tax Line** | A system-generated line (`IsTaxLine=true`) that represents the VAT amount. Hidden from the UI. |
| **IRPF** | Spain-specific withholding tax. **Removed from scope** — Spain is no longer a requirement for the new UI. |
| **IsVATSubjected** | Whether the company is subject to VAT. When false, VAT-related fields are hidden and amount labels change. |
| **LegislationCountry** | Two-letter country code (NL, BE, ES) from the domain — determines country-specific field visibility. |

